-- BOUNDED ONE-TIME BACKFILL (rows in flight at deploy). Rows that were PROCESSING when the previous migration added "sendEnteredAt" read as "sender never entered" and would be requeued and sent again even if their SMTP send was under way. Treat them as "may have sent": the claim time stands in for the entry time. Touches only PROCESSING rows with no value yet (normally zero or one with a serial drain); idempotent (a second run matches nothing). ADDITIVE: data only, no schema change.
UPDATE "email_outbox" SET "sendEnteredAt" = "processingStartedAt" WHERE "status" = 'PROCESSING' AND "sendEnteredAt" IS NULL AND "processingStartedAt" IS NOT NULL;
